Object Recipe Phase 3 Complete — Relationships and Reuse

Implemented recipe v0.3 as a declarative relationship/reuse layer.

Added:
- Versioned v0.3 JSON Schema
- Safe arithmetic expressions and parameter references
- Dimension-derived transforms, offsets, and anchors
- Reusable components
- Explicit exposed anchors
- Nested component instances
- Bounded linear replication
- Bounded radial replication
- Four-torus pyramid assembly test
- Continued use of OBJECT_REGISTRY for geometry generation
- Preserved v0.1 and v0.2 compatibility

Validation:
- 20 Object Recipe tests passed
- 38 total tests passed
- Python compilation passed
- Schema validation passed
- No diagnostics found

Architecture:
- v0.3 flattens reusable components/instances into the
  established v0.2 part/anchor/connection pipeline.
- Primitive generators remain the source of geometry.
- No arbitrary executable recipe content was introduced.

Intentionally deferred:
- Orientation-aware snapping
- Anchor rotation behavior
- Curves/profiles
- Extrusion/revolution
- Boolean geometry
- Physics
- Animation
- Full recipe authoring UI
- Roblox integration
- GLB/GLTF export

Important:
The earlier Phase 3 proposal identified orientation-aware snapping
as a possible next capability. It was not implemented in this
checkpoint and should be treated as a future phase rather than
assumed to be present.